- "Simulate a fictional lost-sales inventory system exactly. There is no stochastic prediction and no missing information beyond the explicit reporting cutoff."
- "Receipts add quantity to stock. Demands consume min(stock, quantity); any unmet quantity is lost (never backlogged). A stockout means strictly positive unmet demand, not merely ending with zero stock."

So each event is either a receipt (stock increases by quantity), or a demand (stock decreases by quantity or to zero; any deficit beyond available stock is lost, but does not affect stock). For stockout, we need to identify event times where unmet demand > 0 (i.e., quantity demanded > current stock at that time). That qualifies as a "stockout event" for the purpose of first_future_stockout_time.

